
<p>Aaron Couch, The Hollywood Reporter:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Patrick Stewart, the sophisticated actor who brought a
Shakespearean touch to <em>Star Trek</em> and <em>X-Men</em> as he made an
otherworldly transformation from British stage veteran to sci-fi
icon, has died. He was 86.</p>

<p>Stewart died Wednesday at his home in Los Angeles following “a
brief and poignant journey with Alzheimer’s disease and Lewy body
dementia,” longtime spokesperson Kelly Bush Novak announced.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>There’s an old adage that everyone’s favorite SNL cast is the one from their teenage years. It’s probably true for <em>Star Trek</em> too. My favorite is The Next Generation and it’s not even close. Stewart’s Jean-Luc Picard was just so fucking cool. Smart, wise, firm, curious, empathetic, and just fucking cool. Those same adjectives seemingly all apply to Stewart himself.</p>

